    "pre_update_notes": "A minor release on top of 2.1.0: System \u2192 Migration moves a whole shop to another server with one encrypted .oeparts file (export, import, one-time download links), the web installer can import an existing site, and System \u2192 Site mode keeps a just-moved copy safe until it is checked. It applies 2 small additive database migrations (one table for one-time download links, and two new permissions) \u2014 nothing in your products, orders, invoices, payments or customers is changed or removed. Update from a single browser tab and leave the update page open until it finishes.",
    "post_update_notes": "After the update: open System \u2192 Migration (super admins have the new 'export migration' and 'import migration' permissions). Nothing is exported, imported or replaced until you start it. To run a 'freeze' export from the admin page, add `migration` to your queue worker command (--queue=migration,critical,default,low) and restart the worker; without it the page shows the exact command to run on the server instead. The new settings are optional and are listed, commented out, in .env.example.",
